{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MDyRYWJ12E6JKBQoJd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0169N8dEFpRd9TsuLvjfnEr2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","offset":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":401,"cache_read_input_tokens":73610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":401},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ede17c71-4de9-46d8-a551-1a7b4d58c296","uuid":"4bcd6ceb-13f6-452f-b379-c016b0b88bcb","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:56:18.499Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MDy9AfGup4TYMKwcP4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0169N8dEFpRd9TsuLvjfnEr2":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","offset":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0169N8dEFpRd9TsuLvjfnEr2","type":"tool_result","content":"60\tIn the browser, holes bind by position:\n61\t\n62\t- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n63\t- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n64\t  that attribute; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` removes it.\n65\t- A signal or function in child position is a **reactive region**.\n66\t- `on<event>` with a function becomes a listener.\n67\t- Anything else is static.\n68\t\n69\t`mount(container, markup)` **adopts** existing children: it walks the\n70\tmarkup against the DOM in document order, binds, and creates no nodes.\n71\tAn empty container gets new nodes. It returns a dispose function that\n72\tstops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Mounting\n73\ttwice on one container throws.\n74\t\n75\tHosts are opaque. Adoption and reconciliation never descend into a\n76\thost's own markup, only into its marked children range, if any.\n77\t\n78\tWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\n79\tmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\n80\tare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\n81\tkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n82\t\n83\tStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\n84\tstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\n85\tand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\n86\tdevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n87\t\n88\t## Trade-offs\n89\t\n90\tApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\n91\tlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\n92\tpay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n93\t\n94\tValue updates go straight through signals with no diffing. Only\n95\tstructural changes (conditionals, lists) pay for a morph, and only over\n96\tthe affected region.\n97\t\n98\tChanging the return type of `html` from string to markup is a breaking\n99\tchange. It is acceptable at 0.0.x, and callers convert explicitly.\n100\t\n101\tComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\n102\tused, and nothing where it is not.\n103\t\n104\tTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\n105\tcomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\n106\ta host's markup.\n107\t\n108\t## Consequences\n109\t\n110\tADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\n111\tis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\n112\tentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n113\t\n114\tADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\n115\tcreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n116\t`client: true` or the keep list.\n117\t\n118\tAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\n119\tlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\n120\tnot the attribute.\n121\t\n122\tThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\n123\tcondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n124\t`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n125\t\n126\tThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\n127\thydration example uses it.\n128\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ede17c71-4de9-46d8-a551-1a7b4d58c296","uuid":"84c7704f-4c14-4e60-803f-12cc9aa8bc0c","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:56:18.514Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","content":"In the browser, holes bind by position:\n\n- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n  that attribute; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` removes it.\n- A signal or function in child position is a **reactive region**.\n- `on<event>` with a function becomes a listener.\n- Anything else is static.\n\n`mount(container, markup)` **adopts** existing children: it walks the\nmarkup against the DOM in document order, binds, and creates no nodes.\nAn empty container gets new nodes. It returns a dispose function that\nstops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Mounting\ntwice on one container throws.\n\nHosts are opaque. Adoption and reconciliation never descend into a\nhost's own markup, only into its marked children range, if any.\n\nWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\nmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\nare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\nkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n\nStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\nstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\nand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\ndevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\nlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\npay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n\nValue updates go straight through signals with no diffing. Only\nstructural changes (conditionals, lists) pay for a morph, and only over\nthe affected region.\n\nChanging the return type of `html` from string to markup is a breaking\nchange. It is acceptable at 0.0.x, and callers convert explicitly.\n\nComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\nused, and nothing where it is not.\n\nTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\ncomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\na host's markup.\n\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n\nThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\nhydration example uses it.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":60,"totalLines":128}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0169N8dEFpRd9TsuLvjfnEr2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3ME9X1MqyL3ywnXnWpU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EQQrbvUM23ZsGdomNEbyDs","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","old_string":"twice on one container throws.\n","new_string":"twice on one container throws.\n\nCorrection (2026-10-14): \"binds, and creates no nodes\" now holds for\nattributes too. Adoption writes no static attribute values. A bound\nattribute's first run compares against the attribute already there\n(and its presence, for the remove case) and writes only when the value\ndiffers; later runs write as usual. Adopting no longer reloads iframes\nor media.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1292,"cache_read_input_tokens":74011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1292},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ede17c71-4de9-46d8-a551-1a7b4d58c296","uuid":"5d3b67d2-3b42-4f35-a9b8-c037bdcf3d53","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:56:22.139Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3ME9EQ5rkauGoxhVzT6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EQQrbvUM23ZsGdomNEbyDs":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","old_string":"twice on one container throws.\n","new_string":"twice on one container throws.\n\nCorrection (2026-10-14): \"binds, and creates no nodes\" now holds for\nattributes too. Adoption writes no static attribute values. A bound\nattribute's first run compares against the attribute already there\n(and its presence, for the remove case) and writes only when the value\ndiffers; later runs write as usual. Adopting no longer reloads iframes\nor media.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQQrbvUM23ZsGdomNEbyDs","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ede17c71-4de9-46d8-a551-1a7b4d58c296","uuid":"fe0f4fa6-9408-4dcc-ab56-091a172a5da7","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:56:22.202Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-03-passive-adoption-no-attribute-writes/docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md","oldString":"twice on one container throws.\n","newString":"twice on one container throws.\n\nCorrection (2026-10-14): \"binds, and creates no nodes\" now holds for\nattributes too. Adoption writes no static attribute values. A bound\nattribute's first run compares against the attribute already there\n(and its presence, for the remove case) and writes only when the value\ndiffers; later runs write as usual. Adopting no longer reloads iframes\nor media.\n","originalFile":"# ADR-007: Client templater with signal props, reactive regions, and mount\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe `html` templater in `microtags/htm` runs only on the server. It\nreturns a string, escapes interpolated values, and expands components\nthrough their render links. In the browser there is no way to describe\nthe page, so application state lives in each component's own signals and\npage-level behaviour is manual DOM code: query an element, add a\nlistener, assign `innerHTML`.\n\nAn author coming from React or Preact expects one state object, passed\ndown, changed through named functions, with the DOM following on its\nown. To support that, the same page function must run on both sides: on\nthe server to produce HTML, and in the browser to adopt that HTML and\nkeep it in sync with state.\n\nADR-004 says client bundle size outranks ergonomics. A browser templater\nwith binding and reconciliation is real code. The maintainer has waived\nstrict size limits for this work, for the templater subpath only.\n\nAlternatives considered:\n\n- Keep page code imperative and only lift state into one object.\n  Rejected: the DOM would still be wired by hand, which is the problem.\n- Ship a virtual DOM library. Rejected: it re-renders whole trees, and\n  it does not know about microtags hosts or the server's markup.\n- Re-render regions by assigning `innerHTML`. Rejected: it recreates\n  hosts, losing their state and identity.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe core entry exports `Signal` and `Serialized<T>` as types.\n`Serialized<T>` is a shallow unwrap: each property that is a signal\nbecomes its value type, and other properties pass through. No runtime\nserialization helper ships in the library.\n\nEvery host gets a property accessor for each declared prop. Assigning a\nplain value writes the prop; assigning a signal makes the prop read\nthrough to it. A property set before upgrade is picked up at upgrade.\nThis is the only runtime change to the core entry.\n\n`microtags/htm` gains a second module, selected by the `browser` export\ncondition. The import specifier is the same on both sides, with no\nruntime environment check. `html` returns opaque **markup** on both\nsides instead of a string. Server markup converts to its HTML with\n`String()`. Markup, render output, and `raw` stay trusted, so nesting\nnever double-escapes.\n\nOn the server, a signal or function in a hole is evaluated once. In\nchild position its output is wrapped in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->`\nmarkers, and so are children passed to a component. A function-valued\n`on<event>` prop is omitted. A page with no reactive holes and no\ncomponent children renders the same bytes as before.\n\nIn the browser, holes bind by position:\n\n- A signal as a component prop is assigned to the host's prop accessor.\n- A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element is bound to\n  that attribute; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` removes it.\n- A signal or function in child position is a **reactive region**.\n- `on<event>` with a function becomes a listener.\n- Anything else is static.\n\n`mount(container, markup)` **adopts** existing children: it walks the\nmarkup against the DOM in document order, binds, and creates no nodes.\nAn empty container gets new nodes. It returns a dispose function that\nstops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Mounting\ntwice on one container throws.\n\nHosts are opaque. Adoption and reconciliation never descend into a\nhost's own markup, only into its marked children range, if any.\n\nWhen a region re-evaluates, its old nodes are morphed toward the new\nmarkup. Keyed children are matched by `key` and moved; unkeyed children\nare matched by position and tag name and patched. A matching host is\nkept and its props rebound, never recreated.\n\nStripping is unchanged. Creating a component whose render link was\nstripped throws an error naming the tag and pointing at `client: true`\nand the build-time keep list. An adoption mismatch on tag name warns in\ndevelopment and leaves that server subtree untouched.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nApp code gets one state object and no manual DOM work, at the cost of a\nlarger templater subpath. Consumers who do not import `microtags/htm`\npay nothing; the core entry grows only by the prop accessors.\n\nValue updates go straight through signals with no diffing. Only\nstructural changes (conditionals, lists) pay for a morph, and only over\nthe affected region.\n\nChanging the return type of `html` from string to markup is a breaking\nchange. It is acceptable at 0.0.x, and callers convert explicitly.\n\nComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\nused, and nothing where it is not.\n\nTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\ncomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\na host's markup.\n\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n\nThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\nhydration example uses it.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":72,"oldLines":6,"newStart":72,"newLines":13,"lines":[" stops effects and removes listeners, leaving the DOM in place. Mounting"," twice on one container throws."," ","+Correction (2026-10-14): \"binds, and creates no nodes\" now holds for","+attributes too. Adoption writes no static attribute values. A bound","+attribute's first run compares against the attribute already there","+(and its presence, for the remove case) and writes only when the value","+differs; later runs write as usual. Adopting no longer reloads iframes","+or media.","+"," Hosts are opaque. Adoption and reconciliation never descend into a"," host's own markup, only into its marked children range, if any."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EQQrbvUM23ZsGdomNEbyDs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
