{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MGPfrYLEB9x3zo2CPv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adoption no longer writes static attributes. The final `npm test` run passed (296/296), `npm run size` is under every limit, and lint is clean.\n\n[x] A MutationObserver attached before `mount` records no attribute mutations on adopted elements whose attributes are all static\n[x] A bound attribute whose current value already matches produces no attribute mutation during adoption\n[x] A bound attribute whose value differs is written once during adoption, and later signal changes still update it\n[x] An adopted `<iframe>` does not fire a second `load` event after `mount`\n[x] `npm test` and `npm run size` pass\n\n**The change** (`src/htm.browser.ts`):\n1. `_setAttr` takes an optional `keep` flag. With it, the attribute is written only if `getAttribute` doesn't already return the new value. Because `getAttribute` returns null for a missing attribute, the same check covers the remove case.\n2. `_bindEl` and `_bindHost` take an `adopt` flag, and `_adopt` passes `true`. While adopting, static values are skipped. A bound attribute's first run uses `keep`, and later runs write as they did before.\n3. Adoption was also rewriting a host's `key` attribute, so that now uses `keep` too.\n\n**Tests** (`test/index.ts`): four new adoption tests watch attribute changes with a MutationObserver attached before `mount`. They cover static attributes on plain elements and a host, bound attributes that already match, bound attributes that differ, and an iframe that must not reload. I ran them against the old code: three failed as expected. The fourth (a differing value is written once and later changes still apply) already passed there, so it only guards against regressions.\n\n**Size:** my first version put the browser templater at 4.62 kB, 18 B over its 4.6 kB limit. Moving the comparison into `_setAttr` brought it down to 4.59 kB, so the limit stays as it is and `.size-limit.js` is unchanged.\n\n**Docs:** ADR-007 has a dated correction saying adoption writes no attributes whose values already match. I also added a short section to AGENTS.md on how to keep adoption passive and how to test it.\n\n`npm test` serves on a fixed port (8123) that sibling worktrees share, and one run failed with \"address already in use\" while another worktree's tests were running. I worked around it by waiting for the port to free up and rerunning. Parallel runs will keep hitting this until the port is configurable. This is recorded in AGENTS.md and in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is left uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":75687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1210},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ede17c71-4de9-46d8-a551-1a7b4d58c296","uuid":"6369a970-dd59-43a7-9392-5c90afa73881","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:56:57.996Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MGPPzgA75WUfEssNJE"}
